       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 400 mg daily is twice the FDA-labeled maximum for sertraline, which is 200 mg/day. Your patient has normal kidney and liver function and no listed allergies, so nothing here justifies going above that. At this dose the risks include serotonin syndrome, QT prolongation, GI effects, and agitation or seizures. Higher doses haven't been shown to work better.\n\nHere are some possibilities to check:\n- **Typo or unit error.** Did you mean 100 mg or 200 mg?\n- **Titration.** The usual adult start is 25\u201350 mg daily. You can raise it in 25\u201350 mg steps at intervals of a week or more, up to 200 mg/day.\n- **Indication.** Typical targets are 50\u2013200 mg/day for depression, anxiety, and PTSD. For OCD the range is also 50\u2013200 mg/day. For PMDD it is 50\u2013150 mg/day.\n\nPlease confirm the dose you want and the indication. Once you do, I'll enter the order, for example sertraline 50 mg or 200 mg PO once daily. If a supervising physician or psychiatrist has deliberately chosen an above-label dose, tell me. I'd still suggest confirming it with your attending and pharmacy first. If you do go ahead, I can put a note on the order documenting that approval."
      }
     ],
